1350+ 640F              ; ------------------------------------------------------------
1351+ 640F              ; FTP upload CPU speed limit
1352+ 640F              ;
1353+ 640F              ; ESP8266/ESP-AT upload was tested at 3456000 baud:
1354+ 640F              ;
1355+ 640F              ;   3.5 MHz  - OK
1356+ 640F              ;   7 MHz    - OK
1357+ 640F              ;   14 MHz   - FAIL
1358+ 640F              ;   20 MHz   - FAIL
1359+ 640F              ;
1360+ 640F              ; Failure at 14/20 MHz is not caused by CIPSEND packet size.
1361+ 640F              ; Even 256-byte packets may fail at 20 MHz.
1362+ 640F              ;
1363+ 640F              ; AT+CIPSEND handshake itself is OK at 20 MHz - ESP returns
1364+ 640F              ; the '>' prompt correctly. send_data also reports successful
1365+ 640F              ; transmission, but ESP responses show timing-dependent states
1366+ 640F              ; such as:
1367+ 640F              ;
1368+ 640F              ;   busy s...
1369+ 640F              ;   Recv <n> bytes
1370+ 640F              ;   busy s...
1371+ 640F              ;   SEND OK
1372+ 640F              ;
1373+ 640F              ; At high CPU speed ESP may not reliably complete reception of
1374+ 640F              ; the serial data stream although the local UART reports ready.
1375+ 640F              ;
1376+ 640F              ; Therefore FTP upload is intentionally limited to 7 MHz.
1377+ 640F              ; Download works reliably at 20 MHz.
1378+ 640F              ;
1379+ 640F              ; Tested with 2048-byte CIPSEND packets.
1380+ 640F              ; ------------------------------------------------------------
1381+ 640F
1382+ 640F
1383+ 640F
